#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr "Glosario"

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>A</title>"
msgstr "<title>A</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid "Article"
msgstr "Artigo"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An <glossterm>article</glossterm> in the sense of newspapers: special "
"<glossterm>articles</glossterm> are, for example, followups; replies are not "
"<glossterm>articles</glossterm> but Email."
msgstr ""
"Un <glossterm>artigo</glossterm> no sentido dos xornais: <glossterm>artigos</"
"glossterm> especiais son, por exemplo, as respostas a todo o grupo; as "
"respostas ao autor non son <glossterm>artigos</glossterm>, senón correo "
"electrónico."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>C</title>"
msgstr "<title>C</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "Canceling"
msgstr "Cancelar"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete one of your articles from the newsserver: the newsreader generates "
"a special control message to tell the server to delete this article."
msgstr ""
"Eliminar un artigo seu do servidor de novas: o lector de novas xera unha "
"mensaxe de control especial que lle indica ao servidor que elimine ese "
"artigo."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "Crossposting"
msgstr "Crossposting (cruce de listas)"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The posting of an article in several newsgroups; this is very often "
"disliked, because it disturbs the topic-oriented association of the "
"newsgroups."
msgstr ""
"Publicar un artigo en varios grupos de novas; isto non é ben recibido porque "
"interrumpe a asociación do grupo de novas cun tema preciso."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>E</title>"
msgstr "<title>E</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expire"
msgstr "Caducar"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<glossterm>Articles</glossterm> can not be held for eternity because of "
"harddisk limits. Because of this there is usually a program called "
"<application>expire</application> on most computer systems; this program "
"deletes all articles which are older than a configured number of days. "
"&knode; includes this functionality on its own."
msgstr ""
"Non se poden conservar os <glossterm>artigos</glossterm> eternamente por "
"causa dos límites de almacenamento. Por iso existe normalmente un programa "
"chamado <application>expire</application> na maioría dos sistemas "
"informáticos; este programa elimina todos os artigos que teñen máis dun "
"número de días preconfigurado. O &knode; trae esta funcionalidade "
"incorporada."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>F</title>"
msgstr "<title>F</title>"

#. Tag: acronym
#: gloss.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>FAQ</acronym>"
msgstr "<acronym>FAQ</acronym>"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<acronym>FAQ</acronym> is the acronym for <quote>Frequently Asked Questions</"
"quote>."
msgstr ""
"<acronym>FAQ</acronym> é o acrónimo en inglés de \"Preguntas Frecuentes"
"\" (<quote>Frequently Asked Questions</quote>)."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Followup"
msgstr "Respostas a todo o grupo"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An <glossterm>article</glossterm> which is written as an answer to another "
"<glossterm>article</glossterm>."
msgstr ""
"Un <glossterm>artigo</glossterm> que se escribe como resposta a outro "
"<glossterm>artigo</glossterm>."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>G</title>"
msgstr "<title>G</title>"

#. Tag: acronym
#: gloss.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "GNKSA"
msgstr "GNKSA"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<acronym>GNKSA</acronym> is a kind of seal-of-approval for newsreaders; you "
"can get more information at <ulink url=\"http://www.gnksa.org\">http://www."
"gnksa.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""
"<acronym>GNKSA</acronym> é un tipo de selo de aprobación para lectores de "
"novas; pode obter máis información en <ulink url=\"http://www.gnksa.org"
"\">http://www.gnksa.org        .             </ulink>"

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>H</title>"
msgstr "<title>H</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "Header"
msgstr "Cabeceira"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Header of an <glossterm>article</glossterm> contains information about "
"the sender, the subject, and the newsgroup of the article."
msgstr ""
"A Cabeceira dun <glossterm>artigo</glossterm> contén información acerca do "
"remitente, o asunto e o grupo de novas do artigo."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>K</title>"
msgstr "<title>K</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Killfile"
msgstr "Killfile"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a functionality of a newsreader to hide <glossterm>articles</"
"glossterm> of a determined sender or with certain contents."
msgstr ""
"Esta é unha funcionalidade dun lector de novas que lle permite agochar os "
"<glossterm>artigos</glossterm> dun remitente determinado ou cun contido "
"específico."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>M</title>"
msgstr "<title>M</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Message-ID"
msgstr "Message-ID"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <glossterm>Message-ID</glossterm> of an article is a clear mark for the "
"newsserver to identify the article. A <glossterm>Message-ID</glossterm> "
"should not be used twice in the whole usenet for about 2 years; wrong or "
"double <glossterm>Message-IDs</glossterm> could cause problems when "
"forwarding them and could overwrite other articles."
msgstr ""
"O <glossterm>Message-ID</glossterm> (\"ID da mensaxe\") dun artigo é unha "
"marca clara do servidor de novas que identifica o artigo. Non se deb e "
"empregar un <glossterm>Message-ID</glossterm> dúas veces en toda a usenet "
"por espazo duns dous anos; os <glossterm>Message-IDs</glossterm> erróneos ou "
"duplicados poderían causar problemas ao redirixilos e poderían sobreescribir "
"outros artigos."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>N</title>"
msgstr "<title>N</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Newbie"
msgstr "Novato"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Somebody who is new somewhere, in relationship to usenet: somebody who is "
"new to the newsgroup, or new to usenet in general."
msgstr ""
"Alguén que é novo algures; no contexto da usenet, alguén que é novo no grupo "
"de novas ou na usenet en xeral."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Newsgroup"
msgstr "Grupo de novas"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A kind-of bulletin board in the usenet about a special topic or a group of "
"topics. This is where you post your <glossterm>articles</glossterm>."
msgstr ""
"Unha especie de taboleiro de novas na usenet sobre un tema determinado ou un "
"grupo de temas. Neles é onde se publican os <glossterm>artigos</glossterm>."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Newsreader"
msgstr "Lector de novas"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "A program for reading and writing <glossterm>news</glossterm>."
msgstr "Un programa para ler e escribir <glossterm>novas</glossterm>."

#. Tag: acronym
#: gloss.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "NNTP"
msgstr "NNTP"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Network News Transport Protocol; this is the protocol which defines how the "
"articles in the usenet are spread."
msgstr ""
"Protocolo de Transporte de novas na Rede (\"Network News Transport Protocol"
"\" en inglés); é o protocolo que define como se difunden os artigos na "
"usenet."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>P</title>"
msgstr "<title>P</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Port"
msgstr "Porto"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A kind-of address for the application to listen for data on and for "
"connecting to another computer; the standard-port for the connection between "
"the newsreader and the newsserver is 119."
msgstr ""
"Unha especie de enderezo polo que a aplicación escoita os datos e polo que "
"liga con outro computador; o porto padrón para a conexión entre o lector de "
"novas e o servidor de novas é o 119."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "PGP-Signature"
msgstr "Sinatura PGP"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A digital signature; you can use it to determine whether the document has "
"been changed since it was signed or if it is the original text from the "
"author."
msgstr ""
"Unha sinatura dixital; pódea empregar para determinar se se alterou o "
"documento desde que se asinou ou se é o texto orixinal do autor."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "Posting"
msgstr "Publicación"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Either an <glossterm>article</glossterm> which is sent to usenet or the act "
"of sending itself; you are <quote>posting</quote> an <glossterm>article</"
"glossterm> into a newsgroup."
msgstr ""
"Un <glossterm>artigo</glossterm> que se envía á usenet ou o acto de envialo "
"mesmo; un <glossterm>artigo</glossterm> <quote>publícase</quote> nun grupo "
"de novas."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Q</title>"
msgstr "<title>Q</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quoting"
msgstr "Citar"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the act of citing of an article to which you are answering: you "
"quote the original <glossterm>article</glossterm> to make clear which "
"passages of text your answer refers to."
msgstr ""
"Este o acto de citar un artigo ao que se responde: cítase o "
"<glossterm>artigo</glossterm> orixinal para que fique claro a que parte do "
"texto se refire a resposta."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>R</title>"
msgstr "<title>R</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reply"
msgstr "Resposta"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <glossterm>reply</glossterm> is an answer to the author of an article by e-"
"mail."
msgstr ""
"Unha <glossterm>resposta</glossterm> (\"reply\") é unha réplica ao autor dun "
"artigo mediante unha mensaxe de correo."

#. Tag: title
#: gloss.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>S</title>"
msgstr "<title>S</title>"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scoring"
msgstr "Puntuación"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the valuation of an article or a thread."
msgstr "Esta é a avaliación dun artigo ou dun fío."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Signature"
msgstr "Sinatura"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <glossterm>signature</glossterm> is a personal sign of the author which is "
"attached at the end of the normal contents of the article; it is like a "
"visiting card &mdash; very often there are e-mail addresses, a homepage "
"<acronym>URL</acronym> or other personal data. The <glossterm>signature</"
"glossterm> should not be longer than 4 lines. Note that the "
"<glossterm>signature</glossterm> should not be mixed up with the "
"<glossterm>PGP-signature</glossterm>."
msgstr ""
"Unha <glossterm>sinatura</glossterm> é un texto personalizado do autor que "
"se engade ao final do contido normal do artigo; é como un cartón de visita "
"&mdash; con frecuencia inclúe un enderezo de correo electrónico, o "
"<acronym>URL</acronym> dunha páxina web ou outros datos persoais. A "
"<glossterm>sinatura</glossterm> non debería ocupar máis de catro liñas. "
"Lembre que non se debe confundir a <glossterm>sinatura</glossterm> coa "
"<glossterm>sinatura PGP</glossterm>."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: gloss.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "Supersede"
msgstr "Substituir"

#. Tag: para
#: gloss.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the overwriting of an existing article: the newsreader generates a "
"special article with a control message in the header which tells the "
"newsserver to overwrite the existing article with this one."
msgstr ""
"Isto consiste en sobreescribir un artigo existente: o lector de novas xera "
"un artigo especial cunha mensaxe de control na cabeceira que lle indica ao "
"servidor de novas que substitúa o artigo existente por este."
